### Page 1 of 12

```text
MEMORANDUM
TO:
Mayor Patrick Collins, and City Council
FROM:
TJ Barttelbort, Purchasing Manager
DATE:
October 17, 2022
SUBJECT:
Professional Services Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and Paladin
Technologies Inc. for the Camera System and NVR System Upgrades at the
Cheyenne Public Safety Center (CPSC)
______________________________________________
Two (2) Responsive Proposals were submitted under Request for Proposal (RFP) #3-23, for the
Camera System and Network Video Recorder (NVR) System Upgrades at the Cheyenne Public
Safety Center (CPSC) project.
The proposals were received from:
1. Paladin Technologies Inc. Cheyenne, Wyoming.
2. KUBL Group.  Cheyenne, Wyoming.
A proposal was also submitted by Corvinus Group LLC, however their proposal did not contain
acknowledgement of the two (2) issued Addendum, therefore their proposal has been rejected.
Upon review of the two (2) responsive proposals by the evaluation panel, the group has
recommended acceptance of the proposal submitted by Paladin Technologies Inc, for a project
award amount of $53,993.81.
Basis for award was based on a Qualifications based review and scoring of proposals.  Paladin
Technologies Inc, submitted the highest scoring proposal, therefore their sealed pricing envelope
was opened & negotiated.
Funding:
030-15-1540-41-43804 (Special Purpose Option Tax 2012 & 2017 / Buildings)
```

### Page 2 of 12

```text
City of Cheyenne / Professional Services Agreement / RFP 3-23
Camera System and NVR System Upgrades at The Cheyenne Public Safety Center (CPSC)
Page 1 of 7
City Contract No. ____________

PROFESSIONAL SERVICES AGREEMENT
for
CAMERA SYSTEM AND NVR SYSTEM UPGRADES AT THE
CHEYENNE PUBLIC SAFETY CENTER (CPSC)

This Professional Services Agreement (“Agreement”) is made and entered into by and between
the City of Cheyenne, located at 2101 O’Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001 (“City”),
and Paladin Technologies Inc., located at 1003 East Lincolnway, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001
(“Consultant”).  This Agreement shall become effective upon the date of the last signature
affixed hereto.

RECITALS

In consideration of the mutual covenants and obligations herein expressed, it is agreed by and
between the parties as follows:

1.
SCOPE OF WORK
The Consultant agrees to provide services for the Camera System and NVR System
Upgrades At The Cheyenne Public Safety Center (CPSC), in accordance with City of
Cheyenne Request for Proposal (RFP) #3-23, incorporated herein by reference, and the
Consultant’s submitted proposal, incorporated herein by reference.

2.
TIME OF PERFORMANCE
The work included in this Scope of Work will be completed by March 31, 2023.

3.
COMPENSATION
In consideration of the services to be performed pursuant to this Agreement, the
Consultant will bill the City and the City agrees to pay Consultant a not to exceed amount
of Fifty-Three Thousand, Nine Hundred Ninety-Three Dollars, and Eighty-One
Cents ($53,993.81) as stated in Exhibit A – Price Proposal.

4.
CONSULTANT RESPONSIBILITY
In providing services under this Agreement, the Consultant shall perform in a manner
consistent with that degree of care and skill ordinarily exercised by members of the same
profession currently practicing under similar circumstances. Upon notice to the
Consultant, the Consultant will, without additional compensation, correct those services
not meeting such a standard.

5.
COMPLIANCE WITH LAWS
The Parties agree that they will perform their obligations as provided in this Agreement
in accordance with all applicable laws and ordinances.
6.
DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE
By Stefanie Boster at 2:21 am, Oct 17, 2022
```

